test_framework_build.py: gen_manifest.py's schema and refusals; build_ipa.sh's
--prepare-xcode copies project-framework.yml in with DM_FRAMEWORK=1 and project.yml
without it; on a stand-in app and framework, the framework is packed at
Frameworks/DmGame.framework with its resources, its signature carries no
entitlements, the app's keeps the Increased Memory Limit request, and a default
pack has no Frameworks/ entry.

test_framework_link.py (skipped without XcodeGen and an iPhoneOS SDK) builds the
DmGame target from a synthetic Gen with two stand-in modules and reads it back with
otool: __TEXT,__dm<mod>x0, __DM<mod>W,__img, __TEXT,__dm<mod>x1 for each, the NRO
pieces and __DATA,__dm_nro_tab, install name @rpath/DmGame.framework/DmGame, and
the tables/profile/manifest at the framework's root. The generated project shows
the app's Embed Frameworks phase and @executable_path/Frameworks rpath.

test_xcode_workflow.py: --prepare-xcode --framework passes DM_FRAMEWORK=1 to the
build. CI runs the link test in the ios-build job, which installs XcodeGen.

Route C M1, docs/launcher-c-plan.md.

